{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire","id":1555512,"title":"Street versus epic - How do you like your vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-16T20:05:49-08:00","id":1555512,"title":"Street versus epic - How do you like your vampire?","content":"Basically, what the title says.<br /> <br /> There's multiple ways of doing Vampire: The Masquerade with 1st Edition being more about politics in a city and personal relationships with the local undead. Then there's the Transylvania Chronicles end of things where the protagonists have centuries-spanning stories and potential huge changes to the setting.<br /> <br /> Which is your favorite and why?<br /> <br /> How do you achieve the feel of both and what do you attempt to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T21:07:12-08:00","id":1555513,"title":"","content":"I like both street Vampire and epic Vampire, but I tend to lean toward the Epic style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T22:17:52-08:00","id":1555514,"title":"","content":"I dont really see it as a binary.<br /> <br /> I also think what both are tends to be a bit reductive and contradictive anyway. For example 5th presents itself as 'street' but is very selective in how it presents the 'street'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T23:30:20-08:00","id":1555516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1555514#post1555514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont really see it as a binary.<br /> <br /> I also think what both are tends to be a bit reductive and contradictive anyway. For example 5th presents itself as 'street' but is very selective in how it presents the 'street'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I really enjoyed about their handling of street was &quot;Blood Sigils&quot; and the idea with the fall of the Tremere Pyramid that EVERYONE is getting in on magic but not really achieving the epic results that people wanted but creating a crude DIY market that is full of notepads, textbook alchemy, cheap substitutes, and grocery store bought goods that I found far more evocative for the setting. Everyone is involved in the Blood Sorcery trade now and the days of the old ancient wizards and their codes of honor are gone.<br /> <br /> It felt better than almost anything out Mage: The Ascension for how I like magic (ala Hellblazer).<br /> <br /> It's partially why I like Curseborne since it was built with that take on magic from the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T09:32:41-08:00","id":1555536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1555516#post1555516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I really enjoyed about their handling of street was &quot;Blood Sigils&quot; and the idea with the fall of the Tremere Pyramid that EVERYONE is getting in on magic but not really achieving the epic results that people wanted but creating a crude DIY market that is full of notepads, textbook alchemy, cheap substitutes, and grocery store bought goods that I found far more evocative for the setting. Everyone is involved in the Blood Sorcery trade now and the days of the old ancient wizards and their codes of honor are gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this was straight out taken from V20, it's from <i>Rites of the Blood</i>. And it didn't had to blow up the Pyramid to do so (although they're certainly not happy with it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T19:17:11-08:00","id":1555585,"title":"","content":"There was something Ken Hite talked about in GURPS Horror 3rd edition about the idea of Scale and Scope in horror games and stories. A good overview of them are in <a href=\"https://fistfulofwits.com/2019/02/14/scope-scale-stakes-longer-thoughts/\" target=\"_blank\">this short essay</a>, along with talk of a third concept, Stakes.<br /> <br /> I always preferred for my WoD games to start at a fairly moderate scale and scope, then tend to escalate as things progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T19:24:30-08:00","id":1555586,"title":"","content":"I believe it depends more on the player characters and how the story develops itself. You might have something epic but the gameplay might set more appropriately for a street level story and viceversa. An experienced ST must be prepared to change this on the fly just in case.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T15:44:58-08:00","id":1555692,"title":"","content":"I prefer something in between. I like V:tM for telling a story that is about on the level of <i>The Godfather</i> but with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T17:54:09-08:00","id":1555695,"title":"","content":"The current chronicle I am running is very street, but its players, who are all new to the universe, didn't need as much broad knowledge of the game's lore to be as effective as in a sweeping epic tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T05:57:09-08:00","id":1555846,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the Kindred I prefer that even the Epic have a fairly scuzzy feel: the more you achieve as a Vampire, the more you\u2019ll stay trapped in the vicious cycle because a vampire will either be obliged to keep shedding blood to maintain their personal power, shed still more blood to accumulate still greater power, accept that it\u2019s time to dry out and blow away or just plain bleed out.<br /> <br /> (Note that \u201cdry up and blow away\u201d is the Golconda approach, wherein one embraces the serious possibility that there is an actual alternative to being the Curse of Caine in human form).<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, I like VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE best when being a vampire rewards you with a degree of power, but demands that you live in the shadows or burn out when the limelight hits you: rather like being a spy or a gangster or any other sort of conspirator, you have to stay secret from the wider world to stay safe enough to get through another night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T21:52:39-08:00","id":1556113,"title":"","content":"I normally prefer street stuff over the epic stuff in all our games be it Vampire, Mage, Heroes Unlimited or Rifts. I know that I can't do high level global or national intrigue with any real decent skill and choose to stay with stuff that I know I can do well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T03:36:03-08:00","id":1556508,"title":"","content":"I prefer the street level stuff. Much more personal and the characters' ability to do and achive things makes more sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T17:05:54-08:00","id":1556542,"title":"","content":"While I also prefer street level, I feel I have to remind people that WoD vampires are heavy hitters among the Kine.<br /> <br /> You can only go so far pretending your PCs are just like competent-but-low-rank gang members, and not undead monstrosities pertaining to a small and incestuous secret society that rules mortal life from the darkness of the night, each capable on its own right and from the get go to seize power in almost any mortal institution (legal or not), with only their peers as a deterrent.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we have to remember that even a Neonate can completely overtake a whole city if they want to and have mild competence, if they're not impeded by other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T01:21:58-08:00","id":1556549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556542#post1556542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only go so far pretending your PCs are just like competent-but-low-rank gang members, and not undead monstrosities pertaining to a small and incestuous secret society that rules mortal life from the darkness of the night, each capable on its own right and from the get go to seize power in almost any mortal institution (legal or not), with only their peers as a deterrent.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we have to remember that even a Neonate can completely overtake a whole city if they want to and have mild competence, if they're not impeded by other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is going to be a big problem when they do mage 5th an arete 2 mage is able to circumvent or bulldoze a large number of 'street' issues unless a mage conciously chooses not to. They're effectively going to have to labotomise the magic system to the point of being borderline useless if they want to run as 'street'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T14:50:34-08:00","id":1556572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556549#post1556549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is going to be a big problem when they do mage 5th an arete 2 mage is able to circumvent or bulldoze a large number of 'street' issues unless a mage conciously chooses not to. They're effectively going to have to labotomise the magic system to the point of being borderline useless if they want to run as 'street'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they don't have to do much because Mage Revised was the start of the &quot;we should be gritty instead of magic carpet riding Taftani fighting the Technocracy around Jupiter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T19:15:27-08:00","id":1556587,"title":"","content":"Most of my vamp-games turn into, Historical-Games; sure, there's modern-times and all, but, vampires are ageless and immortal; why not use that? Downtime can last weeks, months, years and once, decades. And I make my players RPG drinking-blood and being vampires; they're vampires after all, so, street. <br /> <br /> Other games, I've played in, were dozens of law-enforcement officers are killed, is more than, &quot;Epic&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T20:36:39-08:00","id":1556589,"title":"","content":"For me, they start street-level esque, then escalate into epic territory over time.<br /> <br /> It's an old habit from having DM'd DnD5e (which is a completely different structure), and it's been painful for me to break from that mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","user":"DaFrontlineSpecter","date":".  Original wording was not great. 12-13-2025, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T23:49:20-08:00","id":1556590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556572#post1556572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean they don't have to do much because Mage Revised was the start of the &quot;we should be gritty instead of magic carpet riding Taftani fighting the Technocracy around Jupiter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who played a lot of Mage Revised, I <i>partially</i> disagree.<br /> <br /> While Mage Revised did a lot to bring the game to a street-like approach, it's still far from actually street level. Gritty, yes, but not all that street level.<br /> <br /> It also does that mostly through environment rather than rules. You have less support from your faction (whichever it is), no access to major otherwordly communities and a harder time going to the Umbra, although not by much. While the <i>Avatar Storm</i> adds an extraneous effect that effectively hinders the <b>Sphere of Spirit</b>, overall the only <u>major</u> change in the Magic rules is how easy you get common Paradox. Yet this Paradox also hurts you less because Backlashes became far tamer, so it isn't really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Other changes happened all around, but they're more or less a net zero in power level, give or take personal preferences. And even the changes to Spirit I'd argue aren't that big of a problem. You need more effort to do your shit, but it's also a greater advantage as others also need more effort to deal with your results. Not a complete compensation, but it isn't just a loss.<br /> <br /> Revised Mages are definitely still as powerful as 2nd Ed Mages. The game is grittier and more focused on personal goals, but it's &quot;street&quot; only as much as those goals are, and usually that's not for long.<br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> isn't wrong, they actually have to do a lot if they want to force Mage into being street level even if compared to Revised. What happens is that they may be too incompetent to notice that and still give us a powerful Magic system.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556587#post1556587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my vamp-games turn into, Historical-Games; sure, there's modern-times and all, but, vampires are ageless and immortal; why not use that? Downtime can last weeks, months, years and once, decades. And I make my players RPG drinking-blood and being vampires; they're vampires after all, so, street.<br /> <br /> Other games, I've played in, were dozens of law-enforcement officers are killed, is more than, &quot;Epic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the opposite of what the OP defines as &quot;street&quot; vs &quot;epic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Historical games tend to be games where the PCs have significant impact in the events of the area, frequently over a larger area, and with plots that span centuries, games where the &quot;bigger picture&quot; matters and the PCs are changing the world, for better or worse. That's Epic, regardless of how impressive the scenes are.<br /> <br /> Killing cops by the dozen may be heavier on the cinematic action side, but it's still dealing with local things that don't matter far beyond the people directly involved. You may be an unstoppable threat that gets into Action Movie Scenes every other night, yet barely affect the city beyond a blimp in the mortality rate. That's Street as the plot pertains to your life and immediate vicinity, with little regard for a greater scope.<br /> <br /> At least that's my take of the OP's proposal, Phipps may elaborate if he wants to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T02:41:47-08:00","id":1556601,"title":"","content":"Something which occurs in how they actually do 'street' is that it's very piecemeal (for example 5th hates ethnicity and culture in supernaturals but links with that is a 'street' as it gets ) and what they actually mean is 'shit' and 'your powers arnt really supposed to improve your lot'.<br /> <br /> sometimes I wonder if they'd be happier just having you run <i>Poor people:the shoplifting and lower back pain.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556590#post1556590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who played a lot of Mage Revised, I <i>partially</i> disagree.<br /> <br /> While Mage Revised did a lot to bring the game to a street-like approach, it's still far from actually street level. Gritty, yes, but not all that street level.<br /> <br /> It also does that mostly through environment rather than rules. You have less support from your faction (whichever it is), no access to major otherwordly communities and a harder time going to the Umbra, although not by much. While the <i>Avatar Storm</i> adds an extraneous effect that effectively hinders the <b>Sphere of Spirit</b>, overall the only <u>major</u> change in the Magic rules is how easy you get common Paradox. Yet this Paradox also hurts you less because Backlashes became far tamer, so it isn't really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Other changes happened all around, but they're more or less a net zero in power level, give or take personal preferences. And even the changes to Spirit I'd argue aren't that big of a problem. You need more effort to do your shit, but it's also a greater advantage as others also need more effort to deal with your results. Not a complete compensation, but it isn't just a loss.<br /> <br /> Revised Mages are definitely still as powerful as 2nd Ed Mages. The game is grittier and more focused on personal goals, but it's &quot;street&quot; only as much as those goals are, and usually that's not for long.<br /> <br /> So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> isn't wrong, they actually have to do a lot if they want to force Mage into being street level even if compared to Revised. What happens is that they may be too incompetent to notice that and still give us a powerful Magic system.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively yeah, even in revised the power you're packing is going to demolish most 'street' problems aside from other mages. I'm currently running a OoH who started out as a junkie sex worker with addiction flaw....and matter sphere at 2 . I deliberately didn't take mind because it would force the gm to get meta it and force me to fight it out on my own. With that in mind even with deliberate handicaps I'm effectively able to boost my quality of life to an degree were pretty much all 'street' aspects are manageable and slowly being removed especially at Arete 3 to the point she's becoming an established bonisigus magi.<br /> <br /> Unless your deliberately keep the players down (which will typically result in them getting frustrated) if you're running street your going to climb to the big leagues eventually and start altering the playground, for example her position in the post reckoning Order is growing simply because she can make longevity potions (charms)-which a lot of Hermetics can't do anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens is that they may be too incompetent to notice that and still give us a powerful Magic system.<br /> <br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> And their's no reason to presume they are competent. v5 is really easy to 'break' once you know the system and awakening were still considered obscenely powerful on cofd. Best case they'll make playing one unappealing like the garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T10:05:59-08:00","id":1556612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556601#post1556601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which occurs in how they actually do 'street' is that it's very piecemeal (for example 5th hates ethnicity and culture in supernaturals but links with that is a 'street' as it gets ) and what they actually mean is 'shit' and 'your powers arnt really supposed to improve your lot'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the 5e games <b>hate</b> ethnicity and culture as much as they want to divorce it from some of the poorly handled stereotypes baked into the lore of the early days of the game. Instead of the game doing the heavy lifting with culture and ethnicity, they want the players at the table to handle it in ways that they would deem most appropriate to them. But, I also recognize that I am in a minority of people who have been playing the game since 1e who prefers 5e to the earlier editions, so your mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T11:43:46-08:00","id":1556620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556612#post1556612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that the 5e games <b>hate</b> ethnicity and culture as much as they want to divorce it from some of the poorly handled stereotypes baked into the lore of the early days of the game. Instead of the game doing the heavy lifting with culture and ethnicity, they want the players at the table to handle it in ways that they would deem most appropriate to them. But, I also recognize that I am in a minority of people who have been playing the game since 1e who prefers 5e to the earlier editions, so your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The problem is that this leaves the game fundemently lacking a keystone of 'street' play you may as well remove crime &quot;ask the players to do it&quot; mixed with tokenism is a lazy cop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T16:52:03-08:00","id":1556629,"title":"","content":"V20 rules, 1e/2e setting complete with that late 90's/early 2000's mall goth aesthetics and vibe.<br /> <br /> Full-blown &quot;Trenchcoats and Katanas Supers With Fangs Badwrongfun&quot; in all of its unabashed glory.<br /> <br /> Basically, imagine the polar opposite of V5 and the kind of game that would send the likes of Justin Achilli, Jason Carl, Martin Ericsson, Shane DeFreest, and Kareem Muammar into mouth-foaming rage, lol.<br /> <br /> That's how me and my husband like our VTM games. A lot more like Blade, Underworld, Devil May Cry 1, or Grand Theft Auto with fangs and a lot less pretentious personal horror arthouse fare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 12-14-2025, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T04:09:53-08:00","id":1556638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556612#post1556612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that the 5e games <b>hate</b> ethnicity and culture as much as they want to divorce it from some of the poorly handled stereotypes baked into the lore of the early days of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I call that BS.<br /> <br /> However dubious the game representations were (and they weren't by far the worse around), they were fundamental to the themes of the game as they meant it was trying to explore how it affects a person and their lot in life.<br /> <br /> Not only that, it showed that we exist and have histories that matter. At a time when representation was still exceedingly rare, WoD gave non-white people a lot of it. And more importantly, it improved with time, <i><b>a whole lot</b></i>.<br /> <br /> The game ignoring ethnicity as it is doing just reinforces whatever people already think instead of challenging their assumptions or teaching them something about the world. It's a world where everyone is white unless noted and there's no racism as the setting itself is &quot;colorblind&quot;. Your history and the history of your people changes nothing.<br /> <br /> So, as a person of color myself both for US standards and in my own country: fuck that, fuck v5, if you still think Paradox erasing us from the game is good fuck you too, and if you're also PoC fuck you anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T16:57:55-08:00","id":1556678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556638#post1556638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I call that BS.<br /> <br /> However dubious the game representations were (and they weren't by far the worse around), they were fundamental to the themes of the game as they meant it was trying to explore how it affects a person and their lot in life.<br /> <br /> Not only that, it showed that we exist and have histories that matter. At a time when representation was still exceedingly rare, WoD gave non-white people a lot of it. And more importantly, it improved with time, <i><b>a whole lot</b></i>.<br /> <br /> The game ignoring ethnicity as it is doing just reinforces whatever people already think instead of challenging their assumptions or teaching them something about the world. It's a world where everyone is white unless noted and there's no racism as the setting itself is &quot;colorblind&quot;. Your history and the history of your people changes nothing.<br /> <br /> So, as a person of color myself both for US standards and in my own country: fuck that, fuck v5, if you still think Paradox erasing us from the game is good fuck you too, and if you're also PoC fuck you anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU!!! THIS GIRL FUCKING GETS IT!!!<br /> <br /> I'm also a PoC (though I personally don't like using that term for myself for a variety of reasons) and I couldn't agree more. And to be honest, there's a lot of examples of those who honestly don't mind the more &quot;problematic&quot; or stereotypical works in media so long as it's made obvious that it's fiction or if it's meant as a tongue-in-cheek sort of way. Mexicans Love Speedy Gonzales and all that.<br /> <br /> And like you said before, even at its most stereotypical, Classic WoD/&quot;Legacy&quot; WoD offered a lot of representation in a medium and genre where it was otherwise extremely rare at the time.<br /> <br /> As a side note, one of the biggest reasons I don't like the term &quot;PoC&quot; is because I'm a biracial Black American from the South and &quot;Person of Color&quot; just sounds way too much like a modernized and sanitized way of saying &quot;colored people&quot; to me, and if you know the history of that term and its usage during the days of Jim Crow and segregation, then you'll know that it's definitely NOT cool at all.<br /> <br /> Plus it lumps all non-European/non-white ethnicities and cultures into one over-generalized group as well, which is a whole other can of worms on top of that. But that is just my personal preference and I won't get onto another person's case for using that term for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 12-15-2025, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T06:01:47-08:00","id":1556710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556542#post1556542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I also prefer street level, I feel I have to remind people that WoD vampires are heavy hitters among the Kine.<br /> <br /> You can only go so far pretending your PCs are just like competent-but-low-rank gang members, and not undead monstrosities pertaining to a small and incestuous secret society that rules mortal life from the darkness of the night, each capable on its own right and from the get go to seize power in almost any mortal institution (legal or not), with only their peers as a deterrent.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we have to remember that even a Neonate can completely overtake a whole city if they want to and have mild competence, if they're not impeded by other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> I tend to feel that this should be possible only when the Neonate is mostly-ignored (and the supernatural dismissed) by local authorities: if even a raw vampire doesn\u2019t have much to worry about from mere mortals then the Masquerade makes precious little sense.<br /> <br /> To my mind a well-written vampire needs to be more powerful than any single mortal, but still at least potentially-vulnerable to those who are neither ignorant nor unprepared (and most of all to those who outnumber it): this applies as much to the Kindred as to BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER \u2018foreheads\u2019.<br /> <br /> Otherwise why live in the shadows?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T08:43:44-08:00","id":1556722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556638#post1556638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I call that BS.<br /> <br /> However dubious the game representations were (and they weren't by far the worse around), they were fundamental to the themes of the game as they meant it was trying to explore how it affects a person and their lot in life.<br /> <br /> Not only that, it showed that we exist and have histories that matter. At a time when representation was still exceedingly rare, WoD gave non-white people a lot of it. And more importantly, it improved with time, <i><b>a whole lot</b></i>.<br /> <br /> The game ignoring ethnicity as it is doing just reinforces whatever people already think instead of challenging their assumptions or teaching them something about the world. It's a world where everyone is white unless noted and there's no racism as the setting itself is &quot;colorblind&quot;. Your history and the history of your people changes nothing.<br /> <br /> So, as a person of color myself both for US standards and in my own country: fuck that, fuck v5, if you still think Paradox erasing us from the game is good fuck you too, and if you're also PoC fuck you anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to note on this topic, for all that there are thriving audiences for rpgs around the world, WoD ttrpg rulebooks, supplements, what have you, they're published in English first, and ostensibly their biggest audience by numbers sales wise is the US market (it's certainly not like CoC and Japan). When you make a setting, especially one set so firmly in the modern world, dodge issues of minorities, of ethnicity or present itself as &quot;colorblind&quot; or what have you, it really often just comes off as appealing to the sensibilities and perspectives and senses of safety of a majority as some kind of &quot;default&quot;, ironically achieving much the opposite of the supposed intent of taking that approach in the first place.<br /> <br /> I mean my own issues with the WoD are always going to be that I'm disabled with a variety of chronic health conditions and that Mage thereby is one of the most breathtakingly infuriating, ableist games I've ever read, but if someone can't see that there's something honestly offensive in just erasing ethnicity entirely and replacing it with very shallow representations at best, no idea what to say there.<br /> <br /> We live in an age where cultural consultants exist, where it is not hard to find writers of a given ethnic group particularly, where there should be whole editing processes. Working mortal culture, mortal ethnicity in a deeper way into Vampire should not be viewed as some unclimbable mountain.<br /> <br /> Or, short version: Sinners worked just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T18:47:59-08:00","id":1556738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556678#post1556678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it lumps all non-European/non-white ethnicities and cultures into one over-generalized group as well, which is a whole other can of worms on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I reserve it for when I mean exactly that: the one thing we all get, that is how white Europeans (and those who think to be them) see us in a messed up way. And sometimes uncomfortable terms are needed.<br /> <br /> But I have an idea of what it was like and I'm not that much of a fan, either. I'm a mixed brown Brazilian (being Black here isn't a binary based on noticed black ancestry, it's a spectrum of treatments based on comparative skin color), and I now how those terms are loaded, especially by white discriminating usage.<br /> <br /> Most of all, stereotypes or not, WoD showed from the beginning that lumping us all together doesn't really work, and that ignoring our history and its significance can't good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556722#post1556722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We live in an age where cultural consultants exist, where it is not hard to find writers of a given ethnic group particularly, where there should be whole editing processes. Working mortal culture, mortal ethnicity in a deeper way into Vampire should not be viewed as some unclimbable mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, where we have plenty of examples in the exact same market, and even the same IP, of companies with far less resources doing exactly that.<br /> <br /> There's literally no way Paradox can justify it.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556710#post1556710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to feel that this should be possible only when the Neonate is mostly-ignored (and the supernatural dismissed) by local authorities: if even a raw vampire doesn\u2019t have much to worry about from mere mortals then the Masquerade makes precious little sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly what I meant by mild competence. Anyone who's trying to fight off the whole police force is an imbecile.<br /> <br /> You <b><i>factually</i></b> have everything you need to get there with the starting package. This is not my interpretation, this is what the RAW powers give, <b>absent supernatural obstacles</b>.<br /> <br /> If the character will achieve anything in the end depends on their ability to use this and not make stupid choices. No one said Vampires are or should be unbeatable.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T12:55:55-08:00","id":1556761,"title":"","content":"Wait, this is the case even if the dice go against them? (I admit to being more acquainted with the setting than the actual mechanics: also, I tend to imagine that setting should strongly suggest that NPCs should have to make their own rolls whether or not anybody is watching, which might be rather naive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T21:11:38-08:00","id":1556774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555512-street-versus-epic-how-do-you-like-your-vampire?p=1556761#post1556761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, this is the case even if the dice go against them? (I admit to being more acquainted with the setting than the actual mechanics: also, I tend to imagine that setting should strongly suggest that NPCs should have to make their own rolls whether or not anybody is watching, which might be rather naive).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't reasonably account for your chances of success, you're again messing it up yourself. You won't be successful on everything you do, but accounting for that and acting in a manner to both A) maximize chances and B) minimize risks upon failure isn't as hard as it may sound.<br /> <br /> The setting <b>and the rules</b> also don't assume every action has an attached roll, even actions with defined rolls. Rolls are for dramatic situations where uncertainty makes sense and adds to the story, which tends to happen a lot during actual play, but not so much if you imagine a slow paced story about someone who's ambitious, but playing safe and on the long run instead of trying to solve a murder case in under two hours. It would make for a poor story, but also for a power-grab with very little dice rolls.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the setting simply wouldn't work. Imagine if every working clerk or surgeon had to roll dice for everything they do. That would mean two three things: unreliability, as every action will have a wildly varying number of successes. High failure rates, because for common tasks the rules have far higher chances of insufficient or no success than reality. And high occurrence of big problems as botches are also a far more likely thing than similar disastrous failures IRL. Even under the assumption that rolling dice is an accurate representation of characters' chances (they &quot;roll even without observers), together that overall means most of the basic human work that keeps society as we know it would become impossible as reliability is a key factor.<br /> <br /> And most important, this is <i><b>hugely</b></i> besides the point. The point is that starting Vampire PCs are not only far stronger than normal people, they have resources and abilities mortals can't easily deal with and can't mimic and that make them exceptional for being what their society is: a secret cabal of unseen masters of humanity. However you think of them as mid-rank gangstas, they are hugely tougher than the other gangstas around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T13:52:24-08:00","id":1557380,"title":"","content":"I think a combination of both works best, largely because there needs to be a believable reason for why Elders have maintained their positions for as long as they do. If getting rid of an Elder vampire was as easy as just barging into their office and blowing them away with a shotgun, then the Sabbat would have done so a thousand times by now.<br /> <br /> Fledglings and Ancillae work best as street level, since they're the vampires who are actually in the streets doing all the dirty work. But the power of Elders and Methuselahs should be something that makes the sin of Diablerie all the more tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}